"""
## Purpose and audience

# MCP LSP Integration Specification

**Feature IDs:** #500-510
**Category:** Tooling
**Status:** Implemented

## Overview
Integration tests for the 10 Tier 4 LSP tools.
Validates JSON-RPC structure, dispatch routing, annotations, and error handling.

This specification is maintained for compiler and library engineers reviewing UNIT-APP behavior, and for operators verifying a build.

## Operator workflow

Run `bin/simple test --no-session-daemon test/unit/app/mcp_unit/mcp_lsp_integration_spec.spl` and confirm the Results line reports 0 failed. Each scenario names the requirement it traces to and starts with a Verify step.

## Compatibility and limitations

Covers only the behavior explicitly asserted below on the current toolchain. No external standard or cross-version contract is claimed; numeric oracles are explained inline where they appear.

## Recovery and troubleshooting

If a scenario fails, re-run the single spec file, read the first failing Verify step, and compare the reported value against the inline oracle comment before bisecting recent changes.
"""
use std.spec.{step}
# @manual: primary
# REQ-UNIT-APP-001
# doc-path: doc/01_research/app/
# doc-path: doc/03_plan/app/
# doc-path: doc/04_architecture/app/
# doc-path: doc/05_design/app/
describe "LSP tool dispatch routing":
    """
    ## Tool Dispatch
    Validates that all 10 Tier 4 tools are properly routed in dispatch_tool().
    """
    it "routes simple_signature_help":
        # @req: REQ-UNIT-APP-001
        step("Verify: routes simple_signature_help")
        # @capture: assertion outcomes retained in the spec Results output as evidence
        val tool_name = "simple_signature_help"
        val is_lsp_tool = tool_name.starts_with("simple_")
        expect(is_lsp_tool).to_equal(true)
        expect(tool_name).to_contain("signature_help")

    it "routes simple_rename":
        # @req: REQ-UNIT-APP-002
        step("Verify: routes simple_rename")
        # @capture: assertion outcomes retained in the spec Results output as evidence
        val tool_name = "simple_rename"
        expect(tool_name).to_equal("simple_rename")

    it "routes simple_code_actions":
        # @req: REQ-UNIT-APP-003
